//! VM layer — PRODUCTION CANDIDATE `contracts/PolicyVault.v0.7-root.sil`
//! (contract `PolicyVaultOrgRoot`, generated by `tools/gen_v7_root.js`)
//! driven through the real TxScriptEngine (covenants enabled, real Schnorr).
//!
//! Gate I1 of docs/postlaunch/v0.7-organizational-root-design.md section 11.1:
//! the honest organizational lifecycle, EVERY root-side hostile row of
//! sections 7.8 and 10.8 ported onto the PRODUCTION bytes, the coordinator's
//! D6 rows, the threshold sweep with its one-signature-short refusals, the
//! production-byte encoder integration, and measurement + standardness +
//! MAX_STACK_SIZE headroom.
//!
//! The frozen `PolicyVault.v0.5.sil` / `PolicyVault.v0.6.sil` and the phase-1
//! and phase-2 probe files are never read for anything but the record: this
//! suite compiles the PRODUCTION candidate only.
//!
//! Relative-age note: `this.age >= D` compiles to OpCheckSequenceVerify, which
//! this harness DOES execute (sequence-vs-D and the disabled bit). The
//! CONSENSUS-level UTXO-age rule `check_sequence_lock`
//! (utxo.block_daa_score + sequence - 1 < pov_daa_score) is NOT executed by a
//! script engine and is proven live on testnet-10 at gate I5, not here.

